With the drawdown of US forces in Iraq accelerating, service members are finally beginning to receive a respite from frequent back-to-back tours of duty since 2003 — particularly for Army and Marine Corps units “I think we are going to see a growth in that before we see a decline,’’ Mullen said On Saturday, a 29-year-old mechanic who had deployed four times to Iraq and Afghanistan died of a gunshot wound in Copperas Cove The couple's 6-year-old daughter and 2-year-old son are in the care of Fort Hood's child protective services Since the beginning of the year, there have been 14 confirmed suicides and six suspected suicides of Fort Hood soldiers Grimsley also ordered visits of all soldiers at the rank of sergeant and below who live off post, saying those soldiers could be at risk of falling through the cracks "Everybody's a battle buddy." 

